DELTREE - delete a directory tree››Syntax:› DELTREE [/Y] [/V] [d:]path››Deletes a directory with all its files›and subdirectories, after asking for›confirmation.››Options:› /Y  do not ask› /V  show each directory and file as›     it is deleted››If error 167 appears on a directory›that looks empty, look for hidden›entries with DIR +. A file that was›never closed after a crash can also›keep a directory from being removed; a›disk checker can fix that.››Example:› DELTREE /V D2:>OLD››See also: RMDIR, ERASE›